<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Operational diagnostics | CareCycle</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/app.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/admin.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/ui-consistency.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/diagnostics.css"><script src="/app-nav.js" defer></script></head><body><%- include('partials/app-nav', { activePage: 'admin-dashboard' }) %><main class="app-main diagnostics-page" id="main-content" tabindex="-1"><header><span class="page-eyebrow">CareCycle Administration</span><h1 class="page-title">Operational diagnostics</h1><p>Refresh this page for a current snapshot. Email delivery problems do not undo saved donations or commitments.</p><p><a href="/admin/dashboard">Return to administration</a></p></header>
<section class="surface"><h2>Dependency readiness</h2><dl><dt>Database</dt><dd><%= diagnostics.dependencies.database %></dd><dt>Sessions and shared limits</dt><dd><%= diagnostics.dependencies.security %></dd><dt>Private media</dt><dd><%= diagnostics.dependencies.storage %></dd></dl></section>
<section class="surface"><h2>Notifications</h2><p>Status: <strong><%= diagnostics.notifications.status %></strong></p><% if (diagnostics.notifications.mail) { const notices = diagnostics.notifications; %><dl><dt>Email configuration</dt><dd><%= notices.emailConfiguration %></dd><dt>Queued lifecycle events</dt><dd><%= notices.pendingEvents %></dd><dt>Pending email / retrying / exhausted</dt><dd><%= notices.mail.pending %> / <%= notices.retrying %> / <%= notices.mail.failed %></dd><dt>Sent / disabled / suppressed</dt><dd><%= notices.mail.sent %> / <%= notices.mail.disabled %> / <%= notices.mail.suppressed %></dd><dt>Oldest pending email</dt><dd><%= notices.oldestPendingAt ? new Date(notices.oldestPendingAt).toISOString() : 'None' %></dd></dl><h3>Worker health</h3><% if (!notices.workers.length) { %><p>No recent worker heartbeat. Check that a notification worker is running.</p><% } %><% notices.workers.forEach(worker => { %><p><strong><%= worker.health %></strong> · <%= worker.status %> · heartbeat <%= worker.heartbeatAt ? new Date(worker.heartbeatAt).toISOString() : "Unknown" %> · email <%= worker.mailConfigured ? 'configured' : 'disabled' %></p><% }) %><% } else { %><p>Notification diagnostics are temporarily unavailable. Check dependency readiness and server logs.</p><% } %></section>
<section class="surface"><h2>Requests and delivery counters</h2><p>These counters cover this application process since <%= diagnostics.metrics.startedAt %>. They reset on restart; collect structured logs for deployment-wide history.</p><dl><dt>Requests / client errors / server errors / aborted</dt><dd><%= diagnostics.metrics.requests %> / <%= diagnostics.metrics.clientErrors %> / <%= diagnostics.metrics.serverErrors %> / <%= diagnostics.metrics.aborted %></dd><dt>Response time mean / maximum</dt><dd><%= diagnostics.metrics.durationMsMean %> ms / <%= diagnostics.metrics.durationMsMax %> ms</dd><dt>Email sent / failed / disabled attempts</dt><dd><%= diagnostics.metrics.emailSent %> / <%= diagnostics.metrics.emailFailed %> / <%= diagnostics.metrics.emailDisabled %></dd><dt>Worker batch failures</dt><dd><%= diagnostics.metrics.workerFailures %></dd></dl></section><section class="surface"><h2>Tracing a support report</h2><p>Use the support reference shown on a failed response to find matching structured log entries. Review the error code and registered route. Keep logs private; do not request passwords, reset links, verification documents, or beneficiary details.</p></section></main></body></html>
